    "etymology": {
     "text": "Borrowed from Classical Persian بَاذِنْگَان (bāzingān), ultimately from Sanskrit वातिङ्गण (vātiṅgaṇa).",
     "src": "Wiktionary (kaikki.org)"
    },
    "funFacts": [
     "Through Arabic al-bāḏinjān came Spanish berenjena, Catalan albergínia and French — and German — aubergine."
    ],
    "pitfalls": [
     "Written with ذ (ḏ, as in English ‘this’), not ز: بَاذِنْجَان."
    ],
